  "lostObject": {
    "id": "rose-photo",
    "name": "A faded photograph",
    "text": "A young usherette dancing alone in the empty aisle, laughing. On the back, in Elias' hand: \"Rose, 1929. Same time tomorrow?\""
  },
  "comment": "A duel inside the music box, and a real boss: three hits a life, three lives (losing one winds back the turn of the key; losing the last starts the duel over). Each phase is a turn of her key; its sections are the stanzas of her song. A stanza's first part (beats 0 \u2026 loopFrom) is SUNG ONCE, with the attacks its words announce; the rest is its instrumental REFRAIN, which repeats (mirrored every other time) until her spring is down to the stanza's gate (`until`, default evenly spaced), and then the song goes on. So the words always match what happens, however long the fight takes: a quick player hears the song straight through, a slow one hears refrains. Golden notes (gold) sent back give a hit back. Beats count from the start of each stanza. PROVISIONAL: the game plays a music box waltz until the Suno song arrives (see MAIN.md: each stanza will be a sung segment + a loopable instrumental segment of the file).",
